WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:11.940
SBOMs can be generated from package manifests, lockfiles, installed dependencies, source repositories, build outputs, packages, and container images.

2
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.280
npm provides an sbom command for supported npm projects and formats.

3
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:26.940
CycloneDX tooling, SPDX tooling, Syft-style tools, SCA platforms, CI/CD platforms, and container scanners may also generate SBOMs.

4
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:34.080
The tool choice matters less than understanding what the tool inspected and what artifact the output claims to represent.

5
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:42.920
Tool output differs depending on whether it reads a lockfile, node_modules, a package manager workspace, a container image, or the final deployed artifact.

6
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:48.300
A source-only SBOM may differ from an image SBOM that includes operating system packages.

7
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:55.760
A lockfile-only SBOM may differ from installed dependencies if the environment drifted or optional dependencies resolved differently.

8
00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:01.780
A bundled application may include code that is no longer obvious from the source dependency tree.

9
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.740
Generation should be repeatable and documented.

10
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:13.440
Record the tool name, tool version, input source, output format, build context, and represented artifact.

11
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:22.580
Tie the SBOM to a specific commit, build, image digest, package version, service release, or customer-delivered artifact.

12
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.280
Do not treat a generated SBOM as automatically accurate.

13
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:34.460
Review scope, completeness, assumptions, and known omissions before relying on it for vulnerability response, license review, or customer sharing.
